@startuml PasstheKeysDefended
title PasstheKeys - defended (passkey-bound DPoP)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantPadding 16
skinparam BoxPadding 12
actor "Victim" as V
box Relay Party domain
participant "Compromised\nfrontend" as VP
participant "Server /\nIdP" as AP
end box
participant "Attacker server" as S
actor "Attacker" as A

== Attacker arms, in its own tab of the site ==
A -> AP : Login
activate AP
AP --> A : nonce
A -> S : nonce
activate S
== Victim tries to log in; signs the attacker's nonce ==
V -> VP : Login
VP -> S
S --> VP : nonce
VP -> V : Passkey?
V --> VP : assertion
VP -> S : assertion
VP -> V : Fail
== Attacker finishes the login ==
S --> A : assertion
deactivate S
A -> AP : /login/finish
deactivate AP
AP --> A : **access_token** (DPoP-bound to the passkey)
== Attacker tries to use it, and is stuck ==
A -> AP : /api/me + DPoP proof?
note right of A : DPoP proof = a fresh passkey assertion,\nkey is in the victim's authenticator
AP --> A : 401, no DPoP proof
@enduml
